{
    "chapter_num": 21,
    "verses_count": 40,
    "paragraphs_list": [
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Warnings on the Journey to Jerusalem"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 1,
                    "num_str": "1",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Now it came to pass, that when we had departed from them and set sail, running a straight course we came to Cos, the following "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "day"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " to Rhodes, and from there to Patara. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 2,
                    "num_str": "2",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And finding a ship sailing over to Phoenicia, we went aboard and set sail. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 3,
                    "num_str": "3",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "When we had sighted Cyprus, we passed it on the left, sailed to Syria, and landed at Tyre; for there the ship was to unload her cargo. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 4,
                    "num_str": "4",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And finding "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "NU the disciples"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "disciples, we stayed there seven days. They told Paul through the Spirit not to go up to Jerusalem. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 5,
                    "num_str": "5",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "When we had come to the end of those days, we departed and went on our way; and they all accompanied us, with wives and children, till "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "we were"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " out of the city. And we knelt down on the shore and prayed. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 6,
                    "num_str": "6",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "When we had taken our leave of one another, we boarded the ship, and they returned home."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 7,
                    "num_str": "7",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And when we had finished "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "our"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " voyage from Tyre, we came to Ptolemais, greeted the brethren, and stayed with them one day. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 8,
                    "num_str": "8",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "On the next "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "day"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " we "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "NU omits who were Paul’s companions"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "who were Paul’s companions departed and came to Caesarea, and entered the house of Philip the evangelist, who was "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "one"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " of the seven, and stayed with him. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 9,
                    "num_str": "9",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Now this man had four virgin daughters who prophesied. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 10,
                    "num_str": "10",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And as we stayed many days, a certain prophet named Agabus came down from Judea. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 11,
                    "num_str": "11",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "When he had come to us, he took Paul’s belt, bound his "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "own"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " hands and feet, and said, “Thus says the Holy Spirit, ‘So shall the Jews at Jerusalem bind the man who owns this belt, and deliver "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "him"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " into the hands of the Gentiles.’ ”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 12,
                    "num_str": "12",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Now when we heard these things, both we and those from that place pleaded with him not to go up to Jerusalem. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 13,
                    "num_str": "13",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then Paul answered, “What do you mean by weeping and breaking my heart? For I am ready not only to be bound, but also to die at Jerusalem for the name of the Lord Jesus.”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 14,
                    "num_str": "14",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "So when he would not be persuaded, we ceased, saying, “The will of the Lord be done.”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Paul Urged to Make Peace"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 15,
                    "num_str": "15",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And after those days we "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "made preparations"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "packed and went up to Jerusalem. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 16,
                    "num_str": "16",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Also some of the disciples from Caesarea went with us and brought with them a certain Mnason of Cyprus, an early disciple, with whom we were to lodge."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 17,
                    "num_str": "17",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And when we had come to Jerusalem, the brethren received us gladly. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 18,
                    "num_str": "18",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "On the following "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "day"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " Paul went in with us to James, and all the elders were present. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 19,
                    "num_str": "19",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "When he had greeted them, he told in detail those things which God had done among the Gentiles through his ministry. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 20,
                    "num_str": "20",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And when they heard "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "it,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " they glorified the Lord. And they said to him, “You see, brother, how many myriads of Jews there are who have believed, and they are all zealous for the law; "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 21,
                    "num_str": "21",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "but they have been informed about you that you teach all the Jews who are among the Gentiles to forsake Moses, saying that they ought not to circumcise "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "their"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " children nor to walk according to the customs. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 22,
                    "num_str": "22",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "NU What then is to be done? They will certainly hear"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "What then? The assembly must certainly meet, for they will hear that you have come. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 23,
                    "num_str": "23",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Therefore do what we tell you: We have four men who have taken a vow. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 24,
                    "num_str": "24",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Take them and be purified with them, and pay their expenses so that they may shave "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "their"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " heads, and that all may know that those things of which they were informed concerning you are nothing, but "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "that"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " you yourself also walk orderly and keep the law. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 25,
                    "num_str": "25",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But concerning the Gentiles who believe, we have written "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "and"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " decided "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "NU omits that they should observe no such thing, except"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "that they should observe no such thing, except that they should keep themselves from "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "things"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " offered to idols, from blood, from things strangled, and from "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "fornication"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "sexual immorality.”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Arrested in the Temple"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 26,
                    "num_str": "26",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then Paul took the men, and the next day, having been purified with them, entered the temple to announce the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "completion"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "expiration of the days of purification, at which time an offering should be made for each one of them."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 27,
                    "num_str": "27",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Now when the seven days were almost ended, the Jews from Asia, seeing him in the temple, stirred up the whole crowd and laid hands on him, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 28,
                    "num_str": "28",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "crying out, “Men of Israel, help! This is the man who teaches all "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "men"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " everywhere against the people, the law, and this place; and furthermore he also brought Greeks into the temple and has defiled this holy place.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 29,
                    "num_str": "29",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "(For they had "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "M omits previously"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "previously seen Trophimus the Ephesian with him in the city, whom they supposed that Paul had brought into the temple.)"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 30,
                    "num_str": "30",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And all the city was disturbed; and the people ran together, seized Paul, and dragged him out of the temple; and immediately the doors were shut. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 31,
                    "num_str": "31",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Now as they were seeking to kill him, news came to the commander of the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "cohort"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "garrison that all Jerusalem was in an uproar. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 32,
                    "num_str": "32",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "He immediately took soldiers and centurions, and ran down to them. And when they saw the commander and the soldiers, they stopped beating Paul. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 33,
                    "num_str": "33",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then the commander came near and took him, and commanded "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "him"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " to be bound with two chains; and he asked who he was and what he had done. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 34,
                    "num_str": "34",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And some among the multitude cried one thing and some another."
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "So when he could not ascertain the truth because of the tumult, he commanded him to be taken into the barracks. "
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 35,
                    "num_str": "35",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "When he reached the stairs, he had to be carried by the soldiers because of the violence of the mob. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 36,
                    "num_str": "36",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "For the multitude of the people followed after, crying out, “Away with him!”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Addressing the Jerusalem Mob"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 37,
                    "num_str": "37",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then as Paul was about to be led into the barracks, he said to the commander, “May I speak to you?”"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "He replied, “Can you speak Greek? "
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 38,
                    "num_str": "38",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Are you not the Egyptian who some time ago stirred up a rebellion and led the four thousand assassins out into the wilderness?”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 39,
                    "num_str": "39",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But Paul said, “I am a Jew from Tarsus, in Cilicia, a citizen of no "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "insignificant"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "mean city; and I implore you, permit me to speak to the people.”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 40,
                    "num_str": "40",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "So when he had given him permission, Paul stood on the stairs and motioned with his hand to the people. And when there was a great silence, he spoke to "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "them"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " in the Hebrew language, saying,"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}